@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-task-ids-are-sequential-assigned-by-the-list
+type: decision-log
+title: "Task ids are sequential, assigned by the list"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Tasks need a stable reference that survives a rename. Code under `src/domain/` may not use the clock or
+randomness (r3), so ids cannot be timestamps or random values. The title methods must also accept ids.
+
+## Decision
+
+The list assigns ids from a counter it owns: `task-1`, `task-2`, ... An id is never reused, even after
+a removal. Tasks are stored by id. When a text matches one task's title and another task's id, the
+title wins, so existing callers behave as before.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Ids are deterministic and unique within one list; they are not unique across lists. A task titled like
+another task's id can only be reached by that id through `get`.
